# coin_combinations_ordered:
# CSES 1635, Coin Combinations I (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1635), in our
# own words: given coin values, each positive, each usable any number of times,
# the number of ordered ways to produce the sum target, two sequences of coins being
# different ways when they differ in the order, modulo 10^9 + 7. The input is a
# Scott list of binary naturals (the coin values) and a binary natural target. Part
# of the CSES port's second batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of all sequences of coins
# whose sum is target is built, from the running sum partial_sum = 0 upwards (no sequence once
# partial_sum > target, the empty sequence once partial_sum = target, otherwise each coin put in front of the
# sequences of partial_sum + coin), and its length is counted in binary and reduced modulo
# 10^9 + 7. Its reading is exponential in target even under tabling, since the
# sequences themselves are built and counted; the replacement the family asks for
# is the one-dimensional recurrence ways(partial_sum) = sum over coin of ways(partial_sum - coin), with
# ways(0) = 1, on fixed-width integers modulo 10^9 + 7.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal (the sum
# 10^9 + 7 and the numerals are written with binary_zero, binary_even and
# binary_odd). It β-reduces to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer:
# every recursion ends, since sequences consumes the bounded gap target - partial_sum (every
# coin is positive, so partial_sum grows by at least one and the recursion stops once partial_sum
# exceeds target) and every other recursion consumes a finite list or a binary
# numeral. So the β reduction reaches V; the branches that a Scott boolean
# discards are never read. ../common/binary_modular's binary_modulo, which writes
# no top, is called with the positive modulus only. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by
# the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of
# Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ _ _ binary_modulo
. (λtuple. tuple λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
λ modulus
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself function items. items nil λhead tail. append (function head) λ. self function tail
  )
λ concat_map
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself count items. items count λ_ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ coins target
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self partial_sum
        . binary_less_than target partial_sum nil λ. merge_binary_equality partial_sum target (cons nil nil) λ. concat_map (λcoin. map (cons coin) λ. self λ. merge_binary_plus partial_sum coin) coins
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ sequences
. (λtuple. tuple λcoins target. binary_modulo (count_from binary_zero λ. sequences coins target) modulus)
λ coin_combinations_ordered
. export coin_combinations_ordered
